# CRDC Data Hub CLI Uploader Reference

## Overview

The **crdc-datahub-cli-uploader** is a Python 3.13+ CLI tool that uploads data files and metadata to CRDC Data Hub via S3. It communicates with a GraphQL backend API, validates files locally, obtains temporary AWS STS credentials, and uploads to S3 with progress tracking. CLI version: **4.3**.

---

## CLI Workflow

```
YAML Config → CLI Parsing → Version Check → File Validation (size, MD5, names)
  → Create Batch (GraphQL) → Get AWS STS Creds → Upload to S3
  → Process Manifest (data files only) → Update Batch → Upload Report (TSV)
```

---

## CLI Project Structure (crdc-datahub-cli-uploader)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/uploader.py` | **Main entry point** — orchestrates full upload workflow |
| `src/upload_config.py` | Config parsing (YAML + CLI args), validation, version check |
| `src/file_validator.py` | File validation: size, MD5, naming rules, ZIP/archive support |
| `src/file_uploader.py` | Upload queue with retry logic, progress tracking, statistics |
| `src/copier.py` | S3 copy: multipart for >100MB, manual multipart for >5GB |
| `src/process_manifest.py` | Adds file IDs to manifest, creates `-final.tsv`, uploads to S3 |
| `src/common/constants.py` | Upload types, field names, batch statuses, S3 config |
| `src/common/graphql_client.py` | `get_temp_credential()`, `create_batch()`, `update_batch()`, `get_data_file_config()` |
| `src/common/s3util.py` | S3 upload/download, multipart, token refresh on expiry |
| `src/common/utils.py` | TSV export, UUID validation, size/time formatting, S3 URL parsing |
| `src/common/md5_calculator.py` | Chunked MD5 with dynamic chunk sizing |
| `src/common/progress_bar.py` | Rich-based progress bars (speed, ETA) |
| `src/common/upload_heart_beater.py` | Background heartbeat thread (default 300s) to prevent batch timeout |
| `configs/` | Example YAML configs for data file and metadata uploads |
| `requirements.txt` | pyyaml, boto3, requests, requests_aws4auth, rich, pandas, pytest |

